  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Project for Protection and Assistance for Vulnerable People</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will contribute to the safety, respect and protection of human rights of vulnerable people on the move at local, national and regional levels by improving the capacity of local actors to combat human trafficking in accordance with regulations, IOM international standards and best practices. The project will also strengthen communities through prevention activities and by directly assisting victims of trafficking (VoT) through three specific outcomes that encompass different IOM expertise and complement each other: 1) data collection and information management to understand the phenomenon of human trafficking in Venezuela; 2) conducting awareness-raising, training and coordination activities to better prevent human trafficking; and 3) providing direct assistance to VoTs through case management and shelter support.  This holistic approach to human trafficking in the country helps address the problem from different sides while ensuring protection of the human rights of the victims. All activities are based on international and IOM standards and aim at being coordinated with other actors in the field.</narrative>
  </description>
